# The F-35B's livery: grey, with darker grey fins.
# src/gfx/parts.hpp says how a coat is read.
#
# Each box is in the model's body frame, metres from its origin: +x forward,
# +y starboard, +z down. Measured off the model's own sections
# (assets/models/f35b.mesh): a coat all over is the whole model's box; a
# wingtip's is beyond 88% of the wing's semispan; a fin's is above the
# fuselage's top at the tail, aft of the tail's leading edge; a cheatline's
# is along the fuselage's sides, between the heights given.
#
#    NAME          R   G   B       X0      X1       Y0      Y1      Z0     Z1
name Two greys
coat all-over     95 100 105    -8.00    7.84    -5.63    5.63   -2.94   2.10
coat fin          60  64  70    -8.00   -5.00    -2.30    2.30   -2.94  -0.90
